\title{Feast of St. Francis of Assisi 2026}
\tag{cmc}
\date{2026-10-04}
\author{liamoc}
\quote{
In voluntáte tua, Dómine, univérsa sunt pósita, et non est qui possit resístere voluntáti tuæ: tu enim fecísti ómnia, cælum et terram, et univérsa quæ cæli ámbitu continéntur: Dóminus universórum tu es.\br
Ego autem sicut olíva fructificávi in domo Dómini, sperávi in misericórdia Dei mei: et exspectábo nomen tuum, quóniam bonum est ante conspéctum sanctórum tuorum.
}

\p{This morning I sang with a skeleton crew choir at [All Saints Ainslie](https://www.allsaintsainslie.org.au/), for an, uh, \em{interesting} service replete with all the dogs of the congregation. The animal blessing itself was a bit too \em{Common Worship} for my taste, but it was nice to see all the cute animals. We sang [Brother James' Air](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rsw1gix1CvA): }
\quote{
\poem{
  \line{The Lord's my Shepherd, I'll not want.}
  \line{He makes me down to lie}
  \line{In pastures green; He leadeth me}
  \line{The quiet waters by.}
  \line{He leadeth me, He leadeth me,}
  \line{the quiet waters by.}
  \line{\br}
  \line{My soul He doth restore again;}
  \line{And me to walk doth make}
  \line{Within the paths of righteousness,}
  \line{Ee'n for His own Name's sake.}
  \line{Within the paths of righteousness,}
  \line{Ee'n for His own Name's sake.}
  \line{\br}
  \line{Yea, though I pass through shadows death,}
  \line{Yet will I fear no ill;}
  \line{For Thou art with me; and Thy rod}
  \line{And staff me comfort still.}
  \line{Thy rod and staff they comfort still}
  \line{They comfort still.}
  \line{\br}
  \line{My table Thou hast furnishd}
  \line{In presence of my foes;}
  \line{My head with oil thou dost anoint,}
  \line{And my cup overflows.}
  \line{My head thou dost with oil anoint,}
  \line{And my cup overflows.}
  \line{\br}
  \line{Goodness and mercy all my days}
  \line{Will surely follow me;}
  \line{And in my father's heart alway}
  \line{My dwelling place shall be.}
}
}